UID:3be8d4cd0802ac58@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260725T221423Z
DTSTART:20260716T130000Z
DTEND:20260730T143000Z
SUMMARY:Bastille Day French Film Screenings | AFD Ciné Club | July 2026
LOCATION:M.L. Bhartia Auditorium\, Alliance Française de Delhi\, 72 Lodh
 i Estate\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://afdelhi.org/events/bastille-day-french-film-screenings-afd-ci
 ne-club-july-2026/
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Bastille Day with Alliance Française de Delhi thro
 ugh a curated selection of iconic French films that reflect the richness 
 of French cinema—from timeless classics to contemporary masterpieces. E
 xperience stories of ambition\, resilience\, history\, and identity\, whi
 le celebrating France's cultural heritage on the big screen.\nVenue: M.L.
  Bhartia Auditorium\, Alliance Française de Delhi\nLanguage: French with
  English Subtitles\nEntry: Free and Open to All\n\nLost Illusions (Illusi
 ons Perdues)\n\n16 July 2026 | 6:30 PM\n\nSet in 19th-century France\, Lo
 st Illusions follows Lucien\, a young poet who leaves his provincial home
 town for Paris in search of fame and success. As he enters the glamorous 
 yet ruthless world of journalism and literature\, he discovers the price 
 of ambition and the illusions behind power\, wealth\, and recognition.\n\
 nClick here for Trailer\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nThe Great Escape (La Grande Vadroui
 lle)\n\n23 July 2026 | 6:30 PM\n\nOne of France's most beloved comedy cla
 ssics\, The Great Escape follows two ordinary French civilians who unexpe
 ctedly find themselves helping British airmen escape Nazi-occupied Paris 
 during World War II. Filled with humor\, adventure\, and unforgettable mo
 ments\, the film remains a timeless celebration of courage and solidarity
 .\n\nThe Great Escape\n\nClick here for Trailer\n\nNous / We\n\n30 July 2
 026 | 6:30 PM\n\nAcclaimed filmmaker Alice Diop presents a poetic documen
 tary that journeys through the communities living along Paris' RER B rail
 way line. Through intimate encounters with people from diverse background
 s\, Nous (We) offers a moving portrait of contemporary France\, exploring
  themes of belonging\, memory\, and shared humanity.\n\nClick here for Tr
 ailer\n\nhttps://afdelhi.org/events/bastille-day-french-film-screenings-a
 fd-cine-club-july-2026/
CATEGORIES:film\,cinema
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:62347b227f6806eb@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260725T221423Z
DTSTART:20260722T053000Z
DTEND:20260804T133000Z
SUMMARY:UNSUNG: Celebrating the Extraordinary Grandeur of Smallness
LOCATION:Art Gallery\, Kamaladevi Complex\, IIC\, India International Cen
 tre\, 40 Max Mueller Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/exhibition-unsung-celebrating-extraord
 inary-grandeur-smallness
DESCRIPTION:UNSUNG: Celebrating the Extraordinary Grandeur of Smallness\n
 A photography exhibition curated by Amit Mehra\, photographer\, curator\,
  and founder of the UNSUNG project\, an ongoing initiative that celebrate
 s the lives and contributions of extraordinary yet often overlooked indiv
 iduals.\nThe photographs explore the beauty and significance of lives\, p
 laces\, and ideas that often go unnoticed. Through visual narratives by c
 ontemporary artists\, the exhibition reflects on ordinary people and unse
 en worlds whose stories reveal resilience\, conviction\, and human connec
 tion.\nThe exhibition will be inaugurated on Tuesday\, 21 July’26 at 18
 :00 hrs by Amb Shyam Saran\, President\, IIC\nThe exhibition will remain 
 open daily from 11:00 to 19:00 hrs\n(Collaboration: Srishti Manipal Insti
 tute of Art\, Design and Technology (a constituent of MAHE\, Manipal) and
  Manipal Academy of Higher Education (MAHE)\, Manipal (Institution of Emi
 nence Deemed to be University)\n\nhttps://iicdelhi.in/programmes/exhibiti
 on-unsung-celebrating-extraordinary-grandeur-smallness
CATEGORIES:exhibition\,art\,photography
END:VEVENT
